WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:03.620
Here is an amazingly simple edge that will

2
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:08.460
help tame the curl on any edge
that isn't going to be seamed.

3
00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:14.140
It's perfect for scarves and blankets
and shawls knit in plain Stockinette.

4
00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:15.940
Thanks to Diana Sullivan

5
00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:19.820
for introducing this technique
to machine knitters.

6
00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:21.800
As you are knitting an edge that isn't

7
00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:25.820
going to be seamed,
use a three-pronged tool and transfer

8
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:31.420
needles number 2,
3 and 4 to needle number 1.

9
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:38.880
You'll have two stitches on needle number
one and needle number four is now empty.

10
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:46.200
Pick up the purl bump from the row
below and fill in that needle.

11
00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:50.040
And knit two rows.

12
00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:56.540
Repeat this by picking up numbers 2,
3 and 4, transferring them over

13
00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:04.160
to needle number one and then fill in the
emptied needle from the purl bump below.

14
00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:15.320
Keep repeating this along your
knitting and you'll have an edge that not

15
00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:19.490
only doesn't curl,
but it's decorative too.

16
00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:21.000
I encourage you to give it a try.

